{"schema_version":"1.0.0","id":"cik-0001984060","cik":"0001984060","slug":"atlas-energy-solutions-984060","name":"Atlas Energy Solutions Inc.","ticker":"AESI","exchanges":["NYSE"],"sector":"Crude Petroleum & Natural Gas","sic":"1311","country":"TX","website":"","listed_years":2.4,"first_annual":"2024-02-27","last_filing":"2026-06-03","annual_only":false,"edgar_url":"https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=0001984060&type=10-K","summary":{"sentences":["Atlas Energy Solutions Inc. files with the SEC under \"Crude Petroleum & Natural Gas\", based in TX, and has been publicly reporting for 2 years.","It reported $1.1bn of revenue over the trailing four quarters, down 10.8% against the same quarter a year earlier, at a gross margin of 2.4%.","Listed on NYSE, it funds itself from operations ($105.3m of operating cash flow over the year)."],"generated":true,"note":"Assembled from filing metadata and XBRL figures. Not editorial judgement - and rule 7 asks whether *you* can explain it, so rewrite this in your own words before you rely on it."},"bull":[{"text":"Growth has been positive in 6 of the last 8 year-on-year comparisons, so this is a trend rather than one good quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1984060/000119312526206587/0001193125-26-206587-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-206587"},{"text":"Operating cash flow is positive at $105.3m over the trailing year, so the business funds itself and is not dependent on raising money.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1984060/000119312526206587/0001193125-26-206587-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-206587"}],"bear":[{"text":"Revenue fell 10.8% year on year (Q1 2026 vs Q1 2025). Whatever the story is, it is not currently showing up in sales.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1984060/000119312526206587/0001193125-26-206587-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-206587"},{"text":"Growth is erratic - a standard deviation of 38.4% across 8 comparisons. Lumpy revenue usually means few customers or long contracts, and both make any single quarter a poor guide.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1984060/000119312526206587/0001193125-26-206587-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-206587"},{"text":"Gross margin compressed from 18.3% to 2.4% against the same quarter a year earlier. Either input costs are rising or the company is discounting to hold volume.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1984060/000119312526206587/0001193125-26-206587-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-206587"},{"text":"Gross margin is only 2.4%, so scale has to be enormous before anything reaches the bottom line.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1984060/000119312526206587/0001193125-26-206587-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-206587"},{"text":"The company is loss-making at the operating line (-12.2% margin). Profitability is a forecast, not a fact.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1984060/000119312526206587/0001193125-26-206587-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-206587"},{"text":"The operating loss widened by $47.8m against the same quarter a year earlier - it is getting worse, not better.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1984060/000119312526206587/0001193125-26-206587-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-206587"},{"text":"Officers and directors hold only 1.6% of the shares. There is little alignment between what happens to the share price and what happens to them.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1984060/000119312526254996/0001193125-26-254996-index.htm"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"gross_margin_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Gross mar